    "Rina found herself in Raphael's office again."
    "She had given up on wondering why her mistakes were so bad that she needed intervention from an archangel, but that did not defeat the embarrassment."
    "Looking at him had grown harder with each visit, but at least there was always something new for her to notice thanks to Raphael’s penchant for hoarding antiques. Some of those antiques were somehow older than she was."
    "Even refusing to meet his eyes, she could feel them on her, imagine his exhausted expression. Each time she was called following another one of Uriel’s reports, she swore he lost colour in another strand of hair."
    "He was an archangel with the ability to shapeshift in accordance to his conversation partner’s needs, yet she received his default visage with 10 extra years of aging baked in."
    Ra.c "You are lucky you haven't been kicked out of the army, let alone cast down."
    "His voice was uneven, clearly originally intended to be playful before resignation kicked in."
    Ra.c "Please explain to me, how did your sword end up wrapped around someone's waist?"
    Ri.c "I don't even know anymore. I was just thinking about how much I wanted to win and it started melting. By the time I got ahold of my magic again, it had turned into a belt."
    "He sighed, rubbing his temples. The half-arsed lectures weren't the worst part of these visits, it was how he literally looked down at her. Her stomach churned. He looked at her as though she was a child."
    "So did everyone else."
    Ra.c "I don't know what to do with you."
    Ri.c "I don't know what I would do with me either."
    "At the very least, her self-deprecation earned her a chuckle. Sometimes she wondered if she was only still in Heaven because the other angels needed a laughing stock."
    "If that changed, she wouldn't survive the fall."
    Ra.c "What do I do, what do I do..."
    "He tapped his foot under the desk in tune with his quill pen."
    Ra.c "If your magic is malfunctioning, I should write you off. You shouldn't see the battlefield in your state."
    Ri.c "Please don't! We have a big mission tomorrow!"
    Ra.c "That's my point. You're going to be in enemy territory, it'll be too dangerous. I doubt the demons will find your tricks so funny."
    Ri.c "M-Maybe they'll find me too funny to kill. Please, Lord Raphael, I've been training for this for ages."
    Ra.c "And clearly you'll benefit from more training. I can only heal you so much."
    "He leaned back, his expression stern. It wasn't normal to find that face both disheartening and whatever the opposite of that was, but she supposed nothing was normal about... This... Her core echoed an uneven heartbeat."
    Ra.c "You know how dangerous this mission will be, don't you?"
    "She gulped. She was well aware, but she had been waiting half a millennium for this moment. This wasn't just any battlefield."
    "They had found a section of the Alter World that belonged to a duke of Hell."
    "That duke of Hell was one of Beelzebub's descendents. He was related to the monster who had..."
    Ri.c "I know what I'm getting into. That's why I have to do it."
    "Her eyes were growing wet so she closed them. Tears would do the opposite of persuade him."
    Ri.c "I won't mess up this time, please just let me have a chance!"
    "He regarded her in silence for a moment. She hated to imagine what was on his mind when he looked at her, a tiny cherub too green for her sword. But that was all he would ever see her as if she didn't take this chance."
    Ra.c "... I understand. But please, stick close to your fellow soldiers. There's been reports of a turf war going on in the area with another duke. You need to steer clear of him."
    "That was news to her."
    Ri.c "Another duke? Which one?"
    Ra.c "Asmodeus' son. You're going to be stuck between two lunatics. Are you sure you wish to do this?"
    "Great. Two powerhouse bloodlines. No, she had been prepared for the worst. She needed to do this."
    Ri.c "I'll try to steer clear of him. But I need to watch the Kurona clan fall."
    "It was the only way to honour Roziel."
