    "Maybe he wasn't as helpless as he seemed. Her hand was sticky with his blood, however. They had to find Uriel, fast." 
    "With every step, she half-expected an enemy to jump out at them, however the air remained both silent and stale. If they were human, they wouldn't have survived this long, if at all. This strange world was fiercely protected from humanity, allowed to remain a natural menace."
    "That silence played on her mind however as she honed on the heat, her magic keeping her from crumbling under the elf's light weight."
    "If that silence lingered for too long, she would suffocate."
    Ri.c "Uh... Hey."
    "???" "Hm?"
menu:
    "How did the demons trespass elven territory anyway?":
        jump Chapter1_Choice1_a
    "How are you still alive?":
        jump Chapter1_Choice1_b
    "Do you really think I'm cute?":
        jump Chapter1_Choice1_c

label Chapter1_Choice1_a:
    "???" "Unfortunately, we're kinda weak to fire and ice magic. Have you ever tried to fight a flamethrower with petals? It's an awful experience."
    Ri.c "Figures... Elves have to deal with elemental strengths and weaknesses too, eh?"
    "???" "Yep, but we don't go down without a fight. You should have seen what I did to the poor fucks."
    "She nervously giggled. Hearing something so vulgar from such a graceful face was jarring, but that confirmed it."
    Ri.c "Yeah, I think we saw it. There was blood and petals everywhere."
    "???" "I promise you, half this blood is theirs. But..."
    "He grimaced, his injured arm spasming while his other remained wrapped around his abdomen. She was scared to see what would happen if he moved it."
    "???" "I could still use a doctor. Especially if they're good looking."
    "Rina's core fluttered, her face burning once more. She could attest to that, but if her fellow angels found out, Raphael would be transferring her to another healer."
    Ri.c "W-Well, you won't be disappointed."
    "Despite his vast injuries, the elf grinned."
    "???" "I can't wait."
    "At least he was happy. She stared at the stretch of rocky terrain ahead of her then tensed. She couldn't see the source of it, but the scent of blood was growing stronger. It wasn't just from her companion anymore."
    Ri.c "I-I think we need to run."
    "???" "Away or forward?"
    Ri.c "A-Ahead, I think I sense someone! C-Can you run?"
    "???" "It'll hurt but sure. Let's go."
    "They paced through the mountainous terrain, Rina's internal heat reacting to something on the outside. The air was heating up with power she could never muster."
    "Her fellow soldiers were ahead of them, but they weren't alone."
    jump Chapter1_Scene5

label Chapter1_Choice1_b:
    "???" "Because I'm awesome, of course. It'd take a whole army of those beasts to knock me down."
    "Someone was arrogant, But the fact he was talking to her surely meant something. Could elves be this strong? They were more tribal than any other species she knew of. 'Power in numbers', but she hadn't seen any other elves around."
    Ri.c "If you say so... You look like you've been holding your intestines in this whole time."
    "???" "It's just a scratch. ... A painful one. I'm not used to sitting with pain."
    Ri.c "Don't you guys have healers? I'm surprised you're following me for help."
    "???" "We did have a healer. Then the demons happened."
    "She didn't want to know what that meant. She had seen enough brutality, she could live happily without ever hearing about their antics again."
    Ri.c "A-Ah. Well, our healers are pretty good, they'll get you fixed up."
    "???" "If they're anywhere near as cute as you, they can take their time."
    "Her face was on fire again. She took a shaky breath, silently back chatting the voice in her head currently squealing. Whoever her soul mate was, they had high expectations to meet."
    Ri.c "S-Stop teasing me."
    "Her foot halted, her tiny muscles tensing as the smell of blood grew stronger. That wasn't his, that was in front of them."
    Ri.c "I-I think we need to run."
    "???" "Eh? Why?"
    Ri.c "I sense one of my fellow soldiers, I-I think they're in trouble! C-Can you run?"
    "???" "Not well, but I'll try."
    "He said that, but his movements were ever so slightly faster as they paced through the mountainous terrain. Her internal fire reacted to the increasing heat, from a power she could never muster."
    "Her fellow soldiers weren't alone."
    jump Chapter1_Scene5

label Chapter1_Choice1_c:
    "???" "I don't tend to say things without meaning them."
    "His expression was still pained, yet that smile was undeniably mischievous. Her fire magic flared up, consuming her."
    Ri.c "W-We barely know each other."
    "???" "Don't need to know someone to think they're cute~"
    Ri.c "Y-You're unbelievable."
    "???" "I'm honest."
    "He winked at her. She stared down at the rocky ground, nearly choking on her own flames. She needed to focus on the mission. She needed to find Uriel and save Lumia and Ariel. But this man was making it hard."
    "A quiet girlish voice at the back of her mind squealed."
    Ri.c "You're bleeding out, d-don't you think you have other things to worry about?"
    "???" "I can slowly die and acknowledge I have cute company at the same time. But you might be right."
    "He grimaced, holding his injured arm closer. The other arm remained over his stomach."
    "???" "I haven't gone this long without a healer before."
    Ri.c "A-Are you holding your intestines in? D-Do elves even have intestines?"
    "???" "Oh it's not that bad, I haven't been disemboweled. It just hurts. I'll be fine once I have a good looking healer fussing over me."
    "This man was worrying her. No, she had other things to worry about. The scent of blood in the air intensified, she soon realised it wasn't coming from him. It was ahead of her and she could pick up a searing hot aura ahead of them."
    Ri.c "W-We need to run."
    "???" "Why?"
    Ri.c "I think I sense one of my fellow soldiers. T-They might be in danger. Ca- Can you run?"
    "???" "I'll be slow as hell, but I'll try."
    "He said that yet she found herself having to move her legs faster to keep up. If he wasn't injured, she wouldn't doubt he could sprint across this space in half the time it would take her."
    "That aura ahead of hers was far stronger than her own, but she soon realised it wasn't alone."
    jump Chapter1_Scene5

label Chapter1_Scene5:
    scene alter_world with fade
    show rina at left
    show amadeus dewinged at slightleft
    "There was blood everywhere."
    "The mountain had changed to an open field, one that was once grassy but was now rendered a burning wasteland. Her elven companion let go of her and covered his nose, coughing on the thick dark air."
    "???" "What the hell happened here?"
    hide amadeus dewinged
    show uriel at right
    "She didn't need to think for an answer, it was standing ahead of her armed with a sword and blazing wings. The fight had just been won, but it wasn't without a struggle. Uriel stood over the last twitching demon while his company was tending to a bleeding ally." 
    "None of their soldiers were versed in healing magic, but at least Shalim knew first aid, whispering to the whimpering fresh-faced soldier. He couldn't do anything for their missing arm, but he had cut off the energy flow. Their magic would remain mostly intact."
    "Uriel" "You're alive, Rina. Thank Father for that."
    Ri.c "I-I tried to call for you, we found the duke's territory. B-But Lumia and Ariel are outmatched, they sent me to get you."
    "Uriel" "Sorry, you can see I've been rather preoccupied." 
    "He sighed, sheathing his sword. There was no point trying to keep any of the lackeys for interrogation, they were already crumbling to dust."
    "Uriel" "Did you mark the territory?"
    Ri.c "Y-Yeah, I left an imprint of my magic there. We didn't see the duke just... A lot of thugs like this."
    "Uriel" "Good, lead the way."
    Ri.c "W-Wait, we need a healer first."
    "Uriel" "Don't worry, I've already called Raphael. Shalim and Shahar will stay here with Noel until he arrives." 
    "She was half tempted to stick around. N-No, she would see Raphael again later, she would surely mess things up somehow..."
    Ri.c "That's a relief. Hey-" 
    "She turned around then looked around, her jaw falling slack. The elf had disappeared."
    Ri.c "W-Where the hell did he go?"
    "Uriel" "Where did who go?"
    Ri.c "I-I came here with an elf, he was really badly hurt. He was here just a second ago!"
    "Uriel" "He might have been scared off by all of this."
    "He gestured to the ash and blood before looking at Shalim and Shahar."
    "Uriel" "Did you two see an elf come around here?"
    "Shalim" "Not at all, sir."
    "Shahar" "I can smell fruit, but it's in the other direction. He must have run away."
    "Rina hugged herself, shivering. What on Earth did she do about this? No, she had to get back to Lumia and Ariel. If the elf left, surely it was for a reason..."
    Ri.c "I hope he's okay. Are you ready to go, sir?"
    "Uriel nodded and she started her backtracking, closing her eyes to search for her energy's branding. It was difficult when she was surrounded by gore however. If her magic was stronger, this would be far easier..."
    "Without injured companion however, she could move much faster, the scenery changing swiftly as she honed in on herself. Through the mountain, through the petal-marked portal to the tundra, then finally they made it back to the scarlet grassland."
    "A disgusting stench awaited them."
    show ariel at slightright
    show lumia at slightleft
    "Every one of those shrouded devils was bleeding out into the grass, some of them almost completely disintegrating. It hadn't been without a fight, Ariel chanting so many curses as Lumia bound a seeping stub of a wing with a scrap of his own robes."
    "Uriel" "Good, you're alive."
    "Ariel" "It'd take a lot more than that to kill me. Fuck, I can't believe one of these punks took off one of my wings!"
    "Uriel" "Don't worry, you're not the only one to lose a limb today. I don't think the new recruit Noel will ever want to see a battlefield again."
    "Lumia" "Poor kid. We think the duke is behind these walls, sir. We need reinforcements."
    "Uriel" "Shalim and Shahar will be here soon. I'll call for the others."
    "He stepped around the carcasses and crouched by a tree, clasping his hands. Rina grimaced as she accidentally stepped right into a puddle of ooze and greeted her peers."
    Ri.c "I'm sorry I took so long, I had an... Uh... Little side quest."
    "Lumia" "Side quest?"
    Ri.c "I found an elf. Then I uh kinda lost him. I was trying to get him to safety."
    "Ariel shrugged, holding onto his bleeding shoulder. The wing was too mauled to be repaired. He'd be in the recovery bay for a while."
    "Ariel" "You care too much. But thanks, we were this close to storming the place ourselves."
    Ri.c "Y-You're not planning to still fight, are you? You just lost a wing!"
    "Ariel" "I can handle it. Even at four fifths of my total power, I'm still pretty awesome."
    "Lucky bastard. She sighed, her wings cowering. She hoped that elf man was just as lucky."
    "The air pressure and temperature spasmed as their fellow angels arrived, stray feathers landing in the pooled blood. Some of them blended in, just like the petals."
    "Uriel" "Good, everyone is here."
    "He frowned as he did a head count."
    "Uriel" "Mostly everyone is here. I see the Alter World wasn't too kind to us today. Raphael will be here soon to patch up any of the injured, stay back here if you're injured. This is going to be dangerous."
    "Lumia" "That means you too, Ariel."
    "Ariel" "No. I can keep going."
    "Uriel fixed him with a fiery stare and Ariel gulped."
    "Uriel" "No."
    "Ariel's remaining wings cowered."
    Ri.c "H-Hey sir, maybe I should stay back here too."
    "Uriel" "You're just trying to see Raphael. Get your arse over here."
    "She sighed and moved in line with the other soldiers, waiting for their next briefing. Well, she could always come back with the duke's teeth for Raphael."
    "Maybe today she would get her revenge after all."
    "She just wished she could show off in front of him."
    "Uriel" "Alright, everyone. We don't entirely know what awaits us behind these walls, but stick together. The Alter World has been unpredictable enough today, we don't need it abducting anyone."
    "One of the other soldiers snickered. Uriel shot them a glare and they immediately shut up."
    "Uriel" "It isn't funny. Just getting here has been dangerous. Don't challenge the duke alone if you see him and remember, if you see the other duke, call for me."
    "He said that but she had no idea what either duke even looked like... But the Kurona clan's current duke remained a mystery even in name."
    "Lumia" "Sir, has anyone gathered any more intel?" 
    "Uriel looked expectantly at the other soldiers and one of them feebly spoke up."
    "Soldier" "We did get a potential name from one of his minions, but we're not entirely sure if they were serious."
    "Uriel" "What do you mean?"
    "Soldier" "They said his name was 'Kuro Kurona'."
    "Uriel" "That's just 'black' twice."
    "Lumia" "Sounds like a bad joke."
    "Uriel cleared his throat."
    "Uriel" "Does anyone else have any useful information?"
    "He was met by silence."
    "Uriel" "Move out."
    "They moved forward, the world distorting as they passed through the disarmed gate. Suddenly, they were somewhere far more formiddable."
    "The air within the walls was far colder than outside, not quite tundra but the grassland was frosted over. Far ahead of them was a mansion, one of the walls marked by the same wolf crest as the exterior. And right before it was the barracks, its residents already armed and ready."
    "Rina trembled. If these soldiers used ice magic too, this {b}should{/b} be easy for them. Her peers drew their swords and she prepared her magic."
    "Chaos broke out."
    "The demons were many but numerous were feral, striking out wildly with their weapons and claws when their ice magic was threatened by fire. They were intelligent in that sense but fought like wild animals, some of them even snarling." 
    "The noise bounced between her ears, her magic already whimpering as she attempted to make herself useful. She clenched her teeth and the fireball exploded in an enemy's face, the creature falling back in a smoking heap." 
    "She couldn't let the world distract her, she had to break through to that duke."
    "Some of the enemies were clearly more intelligent than the others, her mind questioning the frost gathering in their palms before the ice magic collided with Lumia's fire." 
    "One demon doing such a thing would be useless but it was entirely a coordinated effort, the collision of equally matched magic producing an explosion of thick fog."
    "It was a risky maneuver but successful, her vision clouded by the aftermath. She could hear her fellow soldiers continuing to battle but some far less confident, just as disoriented as she was. She needed to clear the air, she couldn't fight like this!"
    "As she raised her arms to cast another fireball, another scent clogged her remaining senses. That sweet smell had returned, somehow both nostalgic and frightening. Before she could turn around to see, a hand was already dragging her out of the fog, her squeal muffled as another hand clamped over her mouth."
    "Did she imagine Lumia calling out her name? The swing of a sword came close to her but whoever had a hold on her was fast."
    "Before she knew it, she was pulled into the snowy wilderness."
    scene snowy_forest with fade
    show rina at left
    "Her abductor's nails shed her blood onto the glazed over grass, she could pick up her own scent mixing into that sweet apple aroma. When they were sufficently far enough from the battle, they finally released her allowing her to gasp into the air. Would her peers hear her if she screamed for help?"
    "She hesitantly turned around, her stomach dropping as she locked eyes with him."
    show amadeus at right
    "Rina was met with the sight of the elf, however she realised he was never an elf in the first place. Now she could see his wings, their plumage remiscient of decaying leaves. He still stank of blood, however she realised now his stomach was visible that it had never been harmed at all."
    "That disgusting crimson had belonged to all those demons he had killed. She covered her mouth, her energy threatening to spill out. She had led a fallen angel to her comrades."
    Ri.c "W-Who... Who are you?"
    "???" "Did you forget about me already? I'm hurt."
    Ri.c "I- I thought you were an elf! You're not one of that duke's lackeys, are you?"
    "He snorted, spinning his knife in his hand. It had been freshly used, still dripping with someone else's blood."
    "???" "I'm no 'lackey'. I just wanted to teach that arrogant bastard a lesson." 
    "Her legs trembled, each step back clumsy. He didn't stop her, he just watched with that sly smirk on his pixie-like face. Those warnings came back to her, the warning about the ongoing turf war."
    "Oh no."
    Ri.c "Y-You're the other duke, aren't you? You're Asmodeus' son."
    "???" "Bingo! You worked that out quickly, didn't you?"
    "He rolled his eyes with a chuckle."
    "???" "Well, maybe not. You really thought I was an elf until you saw my wings, didn't you?"
    Ri.c "I've never heard of a fallen angel with nature magic!"
    "???" "Oh, you poor sheltered birdie. Come on, how have you never heard of me? You weren't in a coma for the last 500 years, were you?"
    "She gulped. No, she wasn't. For the last 500 years, she had been trying to prove she was even allowed outside. Every mission had felt orchestrated, her peers trying so hard to keep her out of the worst."
    Ri.c "If you're so confident I should know who you are, then why don't you tell me?"
    "He chuckled, stepping closer to her. There was space to backtrack, yet her feet froze into the ground. Those eyes holding hers, they were so bright but {b}wrong{/b}. His hand reached out and his nails grazed her cheek before sliding down to her throat. It was as though he was marking a target on her."
    A.c "You can call me Amadeus. I was looking for that mongrel, but it looks like your friends might get to him first."
    Ri.c "R-Right, you're after the Kurona duke too, aren't you?"
    A.c "I wouldn't say I'm 'after' him, I'm after his land. I'm not a fan of the cold, but territory is territory."
    Ri.c "S-So why the hell did you trick me?"
    A.c "I just thought it'd be funny."
    "Her face burned, but her wings continued to cower. Amadeus peered at them, his expression smoothing into something more curious."
    A.c "You're quite a weird soldier, aren't you? I thought Heaven's army recruited cherubim, not messengers."
    Ri.c "I-I'm not a messenger, I'm a cherub too!"
    A.c "A cherub with only two wings..."
    "His other hand clutched the knife tight, silently warning her against sudden moves while the hand on her throat moved. It pushed down on one of her wings, knocking her down as she writhed. Her tears burned almost immediately after spilling from her eyes, yet that cold smile told her, he had seen them anyway."
    A.c "Maybe I can use you as leverage. I'll let your friends take out those mutts for me first, though."
    "???" "Who are you calling 'mutts'?"
    show kuro 
    "An icy voice echoed behind them, accompanied by heavy footsteps. They both turned to look, Rina catching a glimpse of Amadeus' sneer through her flickering vision as his grip tighened on her wing."
    A.c "Look who's come to play. It's been a while, Kuro."
    "Rina's limbs liquidated, Amadeus' cruel hold the only thing keeping her stable. There before them was a wild looking man, towering over them and armed with a crimson-stained sword. He smelt like a bleeding wet dog."
    "'Black Black' was real."
    K.c "Don't you have better things to do than tearing the wings off angels?"
    A.c "I'm not tearing any part of her off, that's your family's thing. You're not here to cannibalise my prey, are you?"
    "Kuro rolled his eyes, crossing his broad arms."
    K.c "It wouldn't be cannibalising, we're not the same species. But no, I don't have a taste for anything that can hold a conversation with me. I knew I sensed an angel around here. Shouldn't you be with your friends, lass?"
    Ri.c "I-I was, then this guy dragged me off. You're- You're Kuro Kurona, aren't you?"
    K.c "Just Duke Kuro is fine."
    "He rolled his eye."
    K.c "I don't do the full name thing. What are your friends doing in my territory?"
    "Rina couldn't look him in the eye. This man was who they had been looking for. He had the same iris colour as Beelzebub, cold and callous. Her internal flames flared up, her body was almost a puddle yet it still had the strength to quiver."
    "His fangs were right there, begging to be ripped out."
    Ri.c "We know you've been claiming territory, we can't let you guys keep brutalising the Alter World. We came here to stop you."
    K.c "I knew you didn't come in peace."
    "She jumped as he pointed his sword at Amadeus, his voice lowering."
    K.c "She's on my land. Give her to me." 
    A.c "Get fucked, I found her first. Let me have her or I'll use her as a shield."
    Ri.c "A- A shield?!"
    "Kuro narrowed his eye then shook his head. His powerful wings flexed, his lone eye reflecting the blade's ichor."
    K.c "You're so disgusting. Yamato, where the hell are you?"
    show yamato at slightleft
    "In response to Kuro's booming voice, a third man appeared. Well, it looked like he could barely be called that. He was small, his expression docile as he crept out of the bushes."
    Y.c "I-I'm here, Kuro. What's going on here?"
    K.c "Amadeus is pulling his usual bullshit. Stop the angel from escaping while I kick his ass." 
    Ri.c "E-Eh?!"
    "Amadeus snorted, shoving her down as she shrieked. With his hand free, the flurry of petals appeared once more. Now she knew they were lethal, they looked horribly sharp."
    A.c "I'd like to see you try, bitch."
    "Kuro lunged at him and Rina barely avoided the two men as they hit the ground, Kuro's sword narrowly avoiding Amadeus' ear. The petals danced, one slicing Rina's cheek as she backed away. Yamato caught her from behind, holding onto her tight as he whispered."
    Y.c "Sorry about them. But I can't let you go. You- You understand, don't you?"
    "No, she didn't. Close up she noted Yamato was still taller than her, even if barely. She could easily headbutt him even with him situated behind her, but she didn't fancy her chances being caught between two dukes and... Whatever he was. She peered up at his horns, tilted her head to see his wings. Was he a dragon?"
    Ri.c "W-What's happening?"
    Y.c "I'm as lost as you."
    "She flinched as she felt something dig into her bare shoulder, Yamato nervously chuckled and lightened his hold on her. Just enough to reduce the pain, but not enough to let her flee. She spied his nails, they were pointed and red. Didn't look like blood, maybe they were naturally that colour. Or painted."
    Y.c "Sorry. So, were you and your fellow angels plotting a coup?"
    Ri.c "I-I wouldn't call it that. It's just dangerous for the natives if you demons are fighting over territory."
    Y.c "That's kind of how demons are, sorry. You don't want to get between these two, they've been at this for a while now."
    "More petals flew her way and she squeaked, throwing a wall of fire up to protect herself. Yamato flinched away but didn't let go. What was going on with her comrades? Surely they sensed two dukes around!"
    Y.c "W-Wow, you can use fire magic without burning the forest down. Kuro's kind of banned me from using mine here."
    Ri.c "Divine magic's like that... Haven't you fought an angel before?"
    Y.c "I-I'd prefer not to fight."
    "A pacifistic demon? It would be her lucky day if he wasn't actively keeping her down for a duke to... Wait, what exactly did Kuro want to do with her? She fidgeted and Yamato squeaked, holding her tighter."
    Y.c "Hey, stay still!"
    Ri.c "No, let me go! I don't want some lunatic to keep me prisoner, are you mad?!"
    Y.c "You don't have much of a chance, I'm sorry!"
    "He needed to stop saying sorry, it wasn't doing anything! She gritted her teeth, summoning embers in her palm. Right ahead of her was two dukes fighting, who possibly wanted her for very different reasons. She was scared to find out why."
    Ri.c "Hya!"
    "The fireball flung towards Kuro, however it disintegrated into nothingness inches away from his face. Kuro stared at her, stone-faced, as Amadeus started snickering."
    A.c "Wow, that was pathetic."
    Ri.c "S-Shut up!"
    "Kuro scoffed, dropping his sword then as Amadeus went for the opening he struck him in the face with his fist. Amadeus shoved him off him with a yell, rubbing his cheek."
    A.c "Watch it, you bastard!"
    K.c "Get lost or I'll cut your pretty face open."
    A.c "You can't do that."
    K.c "Want to see me try?" 
    "As Kuro went for his sword again, Amadeus scowled, jumping to his feet then kicking Kuro down as he tried the same. Yamato squeaked and Kuro growled."
    A.c "Alright, take the weakling. I'll come back with Cato and break your front door down."
    "Amadeus went to leave, but not before getting into Rina's personal space. Her limbs froze painfully. There was a knife in his hand, there was a knife in his hand, there was no time for her body to be-"
    "His hand rested on her wing, squeezing the feathers as the wind was knocked out of her. As she gasped, his taunting smile came close to her lips. His hot breath made her squirm."
    A.c "Don't let me catch you away from these two, alright? My knife will have your name carved into it."
    Ri.c "Y-You don't even know my name."
    A.c "Don't be dense, I heard one of your little friends cry for you. I'll see you around, Rina."
    hide amadeus
    "He disappeared into the white forest and her legs collapsed on her, her tears melting the snow around her as Yamato squeaked."
    Y.c "I-Is she going to be alright?"
    K.c "I don't care, but they're going to care. We're bringing her back to Hell with us. They've already found our mansion here." 
    Y.c "That's going to make Heaven really mad at us."
    K.c "That's the point. We have a bargaining chip here. If they try anything, she'll get hurt. So they'll have to listen to us."
    "Yamato peered down, shaking. Between the two horrifying men she had encountered, he seemed the least... Dangerous. But who exactly was he? If he worked for the Kurona clan..."
    "She couldn't stop shivering. The cold and the bubbling dread within her, it was growing too much."
    Y.c "This just feels a bit far..."
    K.c "Yamato. If you want to get anywhere in this world, you need to be a little mean." 
    "He crouched down in front of her. Her tongue was begging to lash out at him, but her mind silenced her. If she wasn't careful, she would just be another splatter in the snow."
    K.c "Come on. Do what I say and you won't get hurt."
    "The world blurred from her tears, a dizziness knocking her sick. Begging to go on this mission had been a mistake. She should have never pleaded with Raphael to let her go."
    "Would she ever see him again? No, she had to be calm. It was the only way to survive."
    "She didn't resist as he dragged her to the feet and through the unforgiving blizzard. Where she was going, it was going to be so much hotter."
    return

label Chapter2_Scene1:
    scene hell with fade
    "The trek to Kuro's true home had been painful. Strangely enough, it was more psychologically so than physically."
    "She had never stepped into Hell, such a place was not one where angels willingly went. Being taken hostage was a common fear amongst Heaven's soldiers, Ariel had always boasted about his rescue efforts. She hoped he would rescue her too."
    show rina at left
    show yamato
    show kuro at right
    "The demons they passed had barely given a glance despite how strange she imagined the situation looked. The moment they had passed through the gate, Kuro had let go of her arm and switched to a more... Unconventional method of leading her. Why hadn't she seen the dog collar coming?"
    Ri.c "This is so humiliating."
    Y.c "I-I'm sorry, at least it isn't made out of chains?"
    Ri.c "That would have been {i}less{/i} embarrassing!"
    K.c "Quit your whining, count your blessings you're coming here intact."
    "That was hardly reassuring. She stared down at the ground, the heat radiated through her boots. If she wasn't a fire angel, maybe it would have burnt her. She grumbled under her breath."
    Ri.c "How do you even bear this, Kuro?" 
    "Kuro stared at her quizzically."
    Ri.c "You're an ice demon, aren't you?"
    K.c "You get used to it. Kind of have to. The closer you get to the core, the colder it is, though."
    "That was because Lucifer and Beelzebub lived there. Why did Hell run so hot when its king and prince were the strongest users of ice magic out there? She peered over to see a small pool of lava. Closer to the core, would it be more solidified?"
    Ri.c "H-How much further is it? Where do you dukes even live?"
    K.c "Not too far from here. The archdemons live closer to the core than us, count yourself lucky you aren't being walked that far."
    "The journey wouldn't be so awful if it wasn't for the leash. She sighed, running what little knowledge she had of this place through her head."
    "The core housed Hell's loyal family - Lucifer, his queen Lilith and Beelzebub. Along with whatever servants they decided to keep around... What was it like to directly serve the devil?"
    "After that, the next layer housed what was colloquially called the 'archdemon mansion'. Whose idea was it to house them all together? Hell had more infighting than any other place in existence."
    "Then there were the dukes. Each of them maintained their own territory, rumours said they needed at least 50 miles between each other. Whether those rumours were true, she was about to find out. Did they go to the same extremes as they did in the Alter World for expansion?"
    "The uncertainty however was which layer they lived in. Ariel had claimed there needed to be 3 separate layers dedicated to the dukes, but that sounded like gossip. When she had never stepped foot here before though, everything sounded like gossip."
    Ri.c "At least I can't hear humans screaming."
    K.c "That's because the torture layer had to be soundproofed."
    Ri.c "... I want to go home."
    Y.c "Sorry, looks like Kuro wants to use you first."
    "Kuro gave him a dirty look. Was it the heat, or was he now red?"
    K.c "Did you have to put it like that?"
    Y.c "Like what?"
    "Kuro stared at him for a moment then shook his head, muttering something incoherent."
    K.c "Never mind. Don't look so scared, angel."
    R.c "W-What the hell are you going to do to me?"
    K.c "Nothing-!"
    "He groaned, rubbing his temple. His other hand remained tight around her leash."
    K.c "I'm not a pervert like Amadeus. You're going to sit in the dark until I've bargained with Heaven, and you'll be grateful about it."
    "She would be grateful if she {b}hadn't{/b} been captured against her will. What did they think they could do with her? If anything, Uriel would just send the retrieval squad."
    Ri.c "You could have taken a more valuable hostage."
    K.c "They would have actually been a struggle to capture."
    "Both of these dukes were scum. She glanced at Yamato and he fidgeted."
    Ri.c "So uh... What exactly are you? Are you Kuro's lap-dog or something?"
    Y.c "N-No, ah..."
    K.c "He's my cousin. He was the son of my uncle, the king."
    Ri.c "W-Wait, you're a prince?!"
    Y.c "L-Last I checked... But in Hell, I'm just a duke. Kinda. I'm still in training."
    "How did one train to be a duke? The dukes were descended from the big guns in some way... Wait, this meant Yamato was-"
    Ri.c "You're- You're descended from Beelzebub too, aren't you?"
    Y.c "Kinda... Well, ah... We're not related to him by blood, but we're the... Great grandsons of Abel, right, Kuro?"
    K.c "Right. Our parents were siblings."
    "The fact they spoke in the past tense... She knew the king of the Kurona kingdom had passed, but were Kuro's parents deceased too? Rina had always struggled to track that family... 500 years after their creation, there were many more generations beyond these two. How did succession work?"
    "No, there was a bigger mystery here."
    Ri.c "You look like a dragon, Yamato."
    Y.c "I am a dragon."
    Ri.c "But you don't look like one, Kuro."
    K.c "I'm not a dragon, that's why. I'm a wolf."
    "She couldn't see any wolf features, but she would take his word for it."
    Ri.c "How the hell did he end up a lizard and you a dog?"
    "Kuro rolled his eye, his voice flat."
    K.c "From our non-Kurona parents, what do you think?"
    "Her head was starting to hurt. She groaned, putting her head in her hands. At least these hadn't been restrained."
    Ri.c "Agh... How much further are we from your house?"
    K.c "We're here." 
    "Oh. She blinked, looking up at the structure before her. She didn't know what she expected from Hell's infrastructure, but it was just an ordinary mansion. Like the one in the Alter World, it had that black wolf crest."
    "What crest did the other dukes have? She looked around, but found no other mansions for miles. Maybe the rumours about territories having to be so far apart were true after all."
    Ri.c "So uh... How far away are we from Amadeus?"
    K.c "He lives in another layer, don't worry about him. If he tries to bother you, I have guards everywhere."
    "He said that, but she could only see a couple. A couple with no faces visible. Kuro's servants really treasured their anonymity, didn't they?"
    Ri.c "Where do you live, Yamato?"
    Y.c "Not around here, these places are way too big for me. I have a little cave further out."
    "She wondered if he meant a literal cave. She shook her head, letting out a shaky breath. Well, this was her new jail for a while. She was not surviving those guards if she tried to escape."
    Ri.c "G-Great. So, are you going to return home then?"
    K.c "Not if he wants his nails intact, I need help locking you up."
    "Two dukes were not needed to restrain her, but she kept her mouth clamped. At least Yamato seemed soft."
    "As soft as one of that bastard prince's descendants could be, anyway."
    "Kuro pulled something over her eyes and she squealed."
    Ri.c "H-Hey, why did you wait until now to blindfold me?!"
    K.c "I thought seeing Hell would frighten you. But I would rather you didn't find your way out anyway."
    "That was backwards logic but she bit her tongue, hearing the door creak open. Without her sight, the tug on her leash seemed more purposeful, albeit not very effective in steering her around. Her other senses worked overtime. She could hear the murmur of confused servants, pick up the scent of freshly cooked meat. They must have prepared it for Kuro."
    K.c "We're going down some stairs, watch your step."
    "If he really cared about her falling, he would let her see. Her legs wobbled, her wings flapping weakly to keep her from falling. Immediately there was a more unpleasant smell."
    Ri.c "W-Why does it smell like blood?!"
    K.c "The last guy I held down here had a big mouth. Don't scream your head off at 3am and you'll be fine."
    "How would she even know what time it was? She felt herself collide with a wall, flinching as Kuro's hand moved to her neck. Off went the collar, but on went something else around her wrists as he forced them upwards. She tugged, finding no reach. {b}Now{/b} she was being restrained. Off went the blindfold and she was met with Yamato cowering behind Kuro as Kuro tore the fabric."
    K.c "There we go. Behave and we won't have any trouble, alright?"
    "She stared around, nausea hitting. The room was awfully bare, dimly lit with just candles to clear the darkness. The stone walls were stained red in places. Besides that, there was little else to note. No bed, just a chair that looked worn down. She gathered it was for a guard to sit in and interrogate whoever was locked up in here."
    Ri.c "Wha- What's going to happen to me now?"
    K.c "Nothing, we'll keep you in here until we get a favourable answer from Heaven. If they're too stubborn though, I might bring in a knife or two."
    "Amadeus wasn't the only stabby one after all. She trembled, jerking her limbs. The chains kept her tightly bound, however. Yamato's expression was uncomfortable."
    Y.c "This feels a bit mean."
    K.c "You have to be mean to be a good duke. If you feel so bad about this, why don't you keep her company? I'll be off to sleep, however. Lock up when you're done."
    hide kuro
    "With that, he was gone. Yamato stared after him, his mouth twitching in distress before he turned to her and bowed."
    Y.c "I am so so {i}so{/i} sorry about him! I swear, you won't be here long!"
    Ri.c "I-I hope you're right. I don't know what Heaven would do, though. They'll probably just send a squad here to fight their way in."
    Y.c "That wouldn't be good. Kuro wouldn't let you go easy."
    Ri.c "I figured so. I-I'm so tired, I just want to lie down. I can't believe there's not even a bed in here."
    Y.c "Kuro isn't known for being very nice to his hostages. But you'd think he'd be nicer, you didn't step on his tail or anything..."
    "The tail she still hadn't seen. She exhaled, closing her eyes. If she switched her consciousness off, this would go faster. She didn't want to deal with... All this."
    Ri.c "I'm going to sleep. Can't say I've tried sleeping upright before, though. You should get going."
    Y.c "A-Are you sure?"
    "She could barely stand his company either. He was kind compared to the other two dukes, but he was still Beelzebub's kin."
    Ri.c "I'll be fine. Leave me be."
    hide yamato
    "He hesitated then slowly nodded, turning his back to her. Soon she was alone in the cell, the candles extinguished by the force of the heavy door slamming closed."
    "This was not how she wanted to get herself involved in the Kurona clan's business. Why was she so stupid to think she could do anything by herself?"
    "She should have never gone off alone, she should have never let herself get tricked by that cruel man who called himself an elf. Was it really a blessing that Kuro had taken her away instead? What would Amadeus have done to her?"
    "Her body shivered and she curled up as best as she could in her forced position. If only her magic didn't fizzle out under the smallest amount of stress. All she could do now was pray that someone saved her." 
label Chapter2_Scene2:
    scene clinic with fade
    "At least she was safe in her dreams."
    "The clinic still smelt of blood, but at least the poor souls here were well taken care of. She lifted her heavy head off the hospital bed, her vision blurry as she peered around. She was in Raphael's office, every little knick-knack a strange source of comfort. The blanket around her chest slipped down, the sight of bandages greeting her."
    "Was this a dream after all or a memory? Her legs felt dead as she carefully lifted herself off the bed, her gaze finally focusing on the silhouette slumped at his desk. The clinic must have been closed for the night. Raphael's head was cradled in his arms, his ears twitching gently in sleep." 
    "Every strand of golden hair reflected the small amount of light filtering through the window. This must have been before she had started stressing him out. Her back ached awfully as she stepped closer, shoulder blades cramping. This wasn't the day he had taken her under his medical care, was it?"
    "She dragged herself over to the window, peering out. No one was around, it was the dead of night. Even in the late hours however, there was the faintest light."
    "She knew this was all in her head, but never so badly had she wanted to return to this office. It was the only place she had left to call home. Her hand trembled on the windowsill, that phantom ache deep in her spirit. Every lecture had felt more difficult than the last, only because she knew the image it painted of her."
    "She wanted to be something bigger than a failure, but she stumbled every time. Would he even be able to catch her anymore?"
    Ri.c "I-If only I could have forgiven him."
    show roziel at right
    hide roziel
    "A red halo flickered in the corner of her eye, she spun around to face the empty corner. For a moment, she thought she saw her."
    Ri.c "Roziel..."
    "No, how could she forgive that cruel prince? If it wasn't for him..."
    "She rested her hand on the edge of the desk. This day was so many years into the past, but she could still remember. Waking up in the middle of the night, bleeding through her bandages in her frenzy but soon mesmorised by this sight."
    "She would still change the past if she could, but she would have been a lot lonelier if she hadn't met him."
    Ri.c "I'm sorry. I-I don't know what to do..."
    "Rina knew she wouldn't receive a response, not from her mentor or the reason for all the pain. Instead, the memories taunted her. Their lives had been perfect until that bastard came along. Everything had changed the moment she had met those cold dead eyes."
    "Time passed in the outside world, if she waited long enough maybe this would all be over. She perched on the arm rest of the chair, her memory's figment of Raphael didn't budge. Instead he remained resting so peacefully, his wings folded over him like a blanket. The lower set of wings gently tapped her with each slumbering motion." 
    "Bunkering down beside him, she curled up underneath them."
    "In Dreamland, she could seek a comfort she could never ask for in reality. It was the only thing stopping her from weeping as she awaited the coming day."
label Chapter2_Scene3:
    scene cell with fade
    show rina at left
    "The candlelight was back when she found herself jossled awake."
    show kuro at right
    "Her vision was struggling to adjust away from the drifting dream, the dark empty walls felt like the false fiction. Her body tensed as she registered someone standing in front of her. He was an imposing figure, his single eye cold like steel."
    Ri.c "K-Kuro-"
    K.c "Finally, you're awake. Are all angels this hard to wake up?"
    "She attempted to kick out, but the chains stopped her far from her target. He rolled his eye, speaking gruffly as he tightened the chains."
    K.c "If that made contact, I would have stabbed you, you know? Don't aggravate your captors in future."
    "Hopefully there wouldn't be a 'future' occurrence. She peered down at her ankles, trembling."
    Ri.c "W-What are you doing here?"
    K.c "I need Heaven to realise how serious I am. Hold still."
    "She gaped at him and he abruptly yanked out one of her feathers, a shooting pain rippling through her as she shrieked. Her magic escaped as cyan mist, her wings cowering to shield her as Kuro stepped away. The feather was still faintly glowing, the quill tainted blue. He stared at it, furrowing his brow."
    K.c "How did that hurt so much? I thought your wings weren't flesh and bone in the same sense as demons'."
    Ri.c "A-Are you mad? They're a part of our spirit, o-of course it hurts!"
    "He rolled his eye, examining the feather. It looked tiny in his large hands. Where his fingerless gloves didn't cover, she could make out callouses and scars."
    K.c "I have my proof, at least. Let's see how many of your angel friends panic when I present them with this."
    Ri.c "W-Whatever you're after, why do you think they'll give it to you? I'm not an archangel or anything, I'm one cherub out of hundreds!"
    K.c "Only hundreds. Your species is so old, why hasn't your population exploded by now?"
    Ri.c "I-It's complicated. Angels have soulmates, we're not supposed to pair up with anyone else."
    "Yet her heart wouldn't remember that. Just thinking about it burned her face with shame. His gaze softened to something more curious as he pressed on."
    K.c "Is it that hard for angels to find their soulmates?"
    Ri.c "When half of us fell and another quarter of us {i}died{/i}, yes. Do you have any idea how hard it is for us to meet our mate then?"
    K.c "Hm... And which part does your soulmate fall under?"
    Ri.c "I-I've never met them, shut up."
    K.c "Then hopefully you have {i}someone{/i} that cares enough to save you."
    Ri.c "One of my friends will probably break in for the sake of it..."
    "Oops, she didn't mean to say that out loud! She couldn't cover her mouth due to the chains, but the look Kuro gave her wasn't particilarly dangerous. More bemused."
    K.c "I'd like to see them try. Getting past the gate isn't easy... Depending on who's in charge."
    "He sighed."
    K.c "Some of the gatekeepers are better than others, unfortunately."
    "She had heard that from Ariel, too. She remembered his peeved rant about the last time he had tried to break in with a squad. Lumia had ended up apparently oogling one of the lady gatekeepers, who had proceeded to kick their asses back to Heaven. His poor wife."
    Ri.c "I've heard."
    K.c "Well, thanks for the angelic history level, I'll be off to send your angel friends a ransom scroll. I've already called Yamato to give you company, don't worry."
menu:
    "I wasn't worried, but thanks":
        jump Chapter2_Choice1_a
    "Why don't you keep me company instead?":
        jump Chapter2_Choice1_b
    "... I'm starting to wish I let Amadeus snatch me instead":
        jump Chapter2_Choice1_c
label Chapter2_Choice1_a:
    K.c "I would tell you not to thank me, but Yamato is too soft to harm you."
    "He rolled his eye."
    K.c "He was already whining my ear off about 'picking on' you. He's far too much of a bleeding heart to be a proper duke."
    Ri.c "I would rather deal with a bleeding heart than a stone heart..."
    "Kuro reached out and ripped out another feather."
    Ri.c "O-Ow!"
    K.c "Consider that a warning. Talk back to me again and it'll be the whole wing. I'll let him in. Be good."   
    jump Yamato_Hangout_Chapter2
label Chapter2_Choice1_b:
    K.c "... You aren't already delirious, are you?"
    Ri.c "N-No, I'd just like to know more about the mean duke holding me captive."
    "Kuro raised his brow then shook his head."
    K.c "Weirdo. If you really want my company, you can wait until I've sent off the ransom mail with your feather. That way they know I'm serious."
    Ri.c "Y-You know you won't get anything valuable out of me, right? No one is going to give Heaven's secrets in exchange for my health."
    K.c "If I'm lucky, you'll be wrong. You sure seem spineless enough to have low self-worth."
    hide kuro
    "Ouch. She watched him leave, still trembling. What on Earth had she asked of him?"
    jump Kuro_Hangout_Chapter2
label Chapter2_Choice1_c:
    "Kuro snorted."
    K.c "Trust me, you don't want that. You'd leave Hell either in a body bag or with a broken halo."
    Ri.c "What do you mean by that?"
    K.c "If he really likes someone, he doesn't harm them. He corrupts them. You'll see what I mean if you ever meet one of his play toys."
    Ri.c "W-What's a 'play toy'?"
    K.c "Stay away from him and you won't have to find out. You don't want to test someone from his family."
    "Right. She somehow forgot Amadeus was one of Asmodeus' children. A shiver ran down her spine. All that flirting, how honest had he really been?"
    K.c "I'll send Yamato in, be good. Or I'll tear out a few more feathers."
    jump Yamato_Hangout_Chapter2
label Yamato_Hangout_Chapter2:
    hide kuro 
    "Kuro left, leaving her trembling against the wall. Hopefully this wouldn't be too traumatising... She barely knew Yamato, was he capable of harm? He seemed disgusted by Kuro's behaviour, after all..."
    show yamato at right
    "She wasn't alone with her thoughts for long, the candlelight flickering indecisively as she watched a shaky foot hold open the door. She saw the wobbly tray in Yamato's hands before she saw his face, flushed with effort as he battled the heavy door. She got the strangest impression that he wouldn't be a very threatening duke."
    Y.c "I hate these enchanted doors... O-Oh, Rina, you're awake!"
    Ri.c "Unfortunately... I was enjoying my trip down memory lane until Kuro woke me up."
    "She sighed and he gave a nervous chuckle, the door slamming closed behind him. The candlelight promptly extinguished and he gave a quiet groan, settling the tray down then turning to the candles. Her brow shot up as he blew them and his breath ignited them once more."
    Y.c "Sorry about that."
    Ri.c "It's alright... Wow, you really are a dragon."
    Y.c "Uh, yeah, I thought we already established that..."
    Ri.c "Y-You know what I mean."
    "She peered down at the tray, her metaphorical heart fluttering at the sight. Sure, she didn't need to eat, but the gifts presented to her warmed her core regardless. She had expected bread and water, not orange juice and chocolate cake."
    Ri.c "You, ah, do remember I'm a prisoner, right?"
    Y.c "Right, but I wanted to make up for Kuro being, um... A bit of a meanie."
    Ri.c "T-Thank you. But am I even allowed out of these things?"
    "She tugged the chains for emphasis and he gave a quiet laugh, resting his hand on the cuff around her wrist."
    Y.c "As long as I lock you back up afterwards, I'm sure he won't mind."
    "She would mind getting locked up again, but at least he was treating her like a person... One of his claws poked into the keyhole, rattling inside until the cuff gave away. He repeated the same with the other cuff and she lowered her arms, rubbing her wrists."
    Ri.c "Thank you... With claws like that, you would be quite good at lockpicking, wouldn't you?"
    Y.c "Sometimes, I'm lucky not to break them though doing that. My claws take a while to grow back."
    "She sat down, hesitantly picking up then sniffing the juice. It didn't smell tainted, it just smelt like juice. She took a sip, peering at him over the rim as he sat down across from her."
    Ri.c "So uh... How are you related to such a rough guy like that? I know you're cousins and all, but you're so different. You're not adopted, are you?"
    "He laughed sheepishly, rubbing his neck. She registered movement, looking to see his tail wagging."
    Y.c "No, we're related by blood. My aunt was quite rough around the edges, she was super tough like Kuro is now. My dad, though... He was a bit of a tyrant until he met my mother, apparently. She never took any nonsense and she always told me to be kind too."
    "So his mother was the dragon... And Kuro's father was the wolf? She furrowed her brow. Here she had assumed their Kurona lineage came from both of their fathers, not just one of them. How many children did Abel's son Cain actually have, now she wondered about it? She sighed. Their family naming conventions were irony enough."
    Ri.c "... I don't understand your family at all. And I thought I knew what was going on."
    Y.c "It does get a bit confusing when there's so many branches of the family, yeah. Do you not come from a big family?"
    "She shook her head. Just thinking about it, her spirit felt cold."
    Ri.c "No, I don't have any family. I was created by God so ah... No parents. Or cousins or nieces or any of those things."
    Y.c "Oh, so you were an only child."
    "A lump formed in her throat. No, she wasn't, but she didn't want to get into it with him, no matter how kind his gestures were."
    Ri.c "I'm a second generation angel, half of us just flat out don't have 'blood relatives'. Same as the first generation. A lot of the other angels just kinda adopted each other."
    "He nodded, his expression one that was clearly meant to be serious but instead looked strangely... Cute."
    Y.c "Like Lord Lucifer and Prince Beelzebub."
    Ri.c "Right. They're brothers from no mother. Or father. Wait, uh..."
    "She paused, fixing him with a confused stare. He stared back at her, his tail continuing to flick in a puzzled manner."
    Ri.c "Do you not call Beelzebub 'grandfather' or something like that?"
    Y.c "It's ah... A bit too confusing to call him anything else but 'Prince', honestly."
    "He furrowed his brow, tilting his head." 
    Y.c "He's our ancestor but not at the same time, kinda. We inherited his magic, not his blood. So I don't think we really consider him family."
    "That was in line with what she had heard... The Kurona clan wasn't a family to Beelzebub, it was a status symbol. A science experiment he despised others meddling in."
    Ri.c "That checks out... So uh, what do you usually do when you're not shadowing Kuro?"
    "A bright grin spread across his face, leaning forward as his tail wagged."
    Y.c "Oh, I like to cook! Kuro claims it isn't 'manly', but he's never complained about anything I've made."
    "Rina poked at the cake with the provided fork. It was spongey, bouncing back with each prod. The chocolate ran over the metal prongs, dripping."
    Ri.c "Did you make this, then?" 
    Y.c "Uh hm. Apparently this is what servants are for, but that takes out the fun of it, don't you think?"
    Ri.c "I don't have servants or know how to cook, so I don't know... Do you need to eat? I don't really have a stomach, it just burns up inside of me."
    "His arm folded behind his head, his smile turning more crooked."
    K.c "Unfortunately, yeah, we do have stomachs. Because we're more human in nature, I guess. Though you angels look really human too..."
    Ri.c "We were apparently the blueprints for humanity..."
    "She sighed."
    Ri.c "Which is why we used to be half-compatible with them, I guess. We can mimic the organs in case a human ever tries to dissect us, but they're not necessary in the same sense as humans'. The only thing we really need is our magic, even our reproductive system is optional."
    Y.c "Really? Then how do you guys usually reproduce?"
    "Her cheeks burned thinking about it. Did she really need to give the talk to a grown man?"
    Ri.c "We ah, have two choices. Either we combine our magic with another angel, or we do it uh... Internally. It's easier to do it externally, though. You don't want to hear an angel in labour."
    "He blushed and bowed his head, chuckling anxiously."
    Y.c "Y-Yeah, I don't think I do..."
    "His gaze darted around the room, clearly searching for a new conversation topic."
    Y.c "So, is Heaven as fluffy as I heard?"
    Ri.c "Depends on where you go, the 'clouds' are really soft but everything indoors has proper floorings. Nicer than this place."
    "She stomped on the cell floor for emphasis."
    Ri.c "There's always at least some light in Heaven too, there's no complete darkness like in Hell or Earth."
    Y.c "Sounds nice... You couldn't get one of your angel friends to take me captive next, could you?"
    "She prodded him and once more he laughed, however the sound was much more relaxed."
    Ri.c "Trust me, you don't want to be an angelic captive. We don't believe in physical torture, but Uriel's really good at hurting your feelings. He's not even malicious about it, he just makes you feel like a naughty kid."
    "Yamato covered his mouth, shaking a little. However, she quickly realised it wasn't fear."
    Y.c "I think I'd still prefer it to hanging around Kuro. I don't like the whole power trip thing. As soon as I earn my title, I'm going home."
    "She tilted her head, her brow knitting. Who was in charge of the Kurona Kingdom in the Alter World right now, actually? Her mind returned foggy and she stored the thought away for now, taking a bite of the cake. The taste of sweet silky chocolate tickled her tastebuds, her eyes widening."
    Ri.c "T-This is really good. Did you learn to make this yourself?"
    "His eyes brightened, his cheeks glowing a soft pink as he beamed."
    Y.c "I'm glad you like it, one of Kuro's servants taught me how to make it. I felt bad about asking her for it all the time so I asked how to make it."
    "He really was a soft man. How did Hell expect to make a duke out of him? She took another bite, closing her eyes. It was a massive stereotype that angels enjoyed desserts, but it was a stereotype for a reason."
    Ri.c "T-Thank you. It makes me feel a bit better about uh... All this."
    "She gestured to the cell walls and he looked at them, nodding a little more stiffly."
    Y.c "I'm sorry about this. I'm sure Kuro will come to an agreement with Heaven soon and let you go. I did tell him he wasn't going to get much out of you, but well... He never listens to me."
    Ri.c "He didn't listen to me either. I just hope nothing bad happens... And I hope Lord Raphael isn't mad at me."
    "She exhaled, her wings twitching. That was misspoken, he wouldn't be {b}mad{/b}, he'd be disappointed. As soon as she stepped into that office, she was going to get the biggest 'I told you so' of her life."
    Ri.c "Oh hey, do you think you could give me the recipe for this?"
    Y.c "I thought you didn't know how to cook."
    Ri.c "I don't, but I haven't been banned from the kitchen yet. I can try."
    Y.c "Okay, just let me get something to write it down on!"
    "She watched him go, the door slamming closed. She looked at the chains hanging above her, waiting to snare her again. She could take the opportunity to run, but that would be dangerous... Especially considering how she got into this mess in the first place."
    "No, she was safer to stay here and see how things played out. Her life wasn't in peril just yet."
    "Yamato soon returned, the most bashful yet cheerful smile on his face as he opened the floodgates and she made notes."
    "Being caught in the company of two members of that cursed bloodline had shook her core. Dark thoughts were still trying to creep in, shaking her handwriting as she attempted to focus."
